cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use, reference, implement, fork, cite, or build upon PRS-001: Provably Rare Standard, please cite this repository and the initial creator."
title: "PRS-001: Provably Rare Standard"
type: "software"
abstract: "PRS-001 defines a cryptographic rarity and provenance standard for digital assets. It enables NFTs, artworks, model outputs, datasets, documents, media files, and other digital artifacts to be anchored to SHA-256 entropy hashes, assigned mathematically verifiable leading-zero rarity classes, committed into public proof structures, and verified through reproducible procedures."
authors:
  - family-names: "Wells"
    given-names: "Brandon"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eternaverse/provably-rare-standard"
url: "https://digitalownership.org"
version: "0.1.0-genesis"
date-released: "2026-04-25"
keywords:
  - PRS-001
  - Provably Rare Standard
  - DigitalOwnership
  - cryptographic rarity
  - NFT provenance
  - SHA-256
  - Merkle proof
